- A successful none-mode report and an approved ai-mode review both complete prerequisites and release dependent tasks. Release alone does not start code: the coordinator/controller must dispatch the next eligible worker. Record every selected task as complete, awaiting human review, waiting on dependencies, blocked/failed or not started, with attempts, evidence and next steps. Checkpoint progress; inspect plan:status and remote state before --resume. Run final integration checks separately. Claim the entire plan complete only when every selected task is done and integration checks pass; never claim that every task must succeed regardless of blockers.

